WHAT TO DO WITH THIS
{{ '=' * 60 }}
Nothing automatically. This report deliberately prints no bump command: for
the images apps.yml leaves untracked on purpose, a one-line `make image-bump`
is precisely the standing recommendation the BUMP PROCEDURE block exists to
prevent. Read the release notes, decide, then follow that procedure by hand.

Before bumping anything, check what the service persists. A bad digest is safe
— the pre-pull aborts the deploy with the old container still serving — but a
bad VERSION is not, and an image that starts fine can migrate a database one
way while every health check stays green.
